  "description": "YUWSUH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C34 H90 N2 O27 Sm6 8+,8(I1 1-),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm5 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm6 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.563-5.246 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.76-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm6(μ3-OH)8(μ6-O)(CH3CN)2(H2O)6.8(C3H6O)11.2]I8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
